course: dictionary
lesson: 2296
title: Colour words and feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Crimson is a colour. It is a deep, strong red with a little blue in it, so it is darker and richer than bright red. In «the Knave of Hearts with the King's crown on a crimson velvet cushion», the words velvet and cushion help you picture that soft, rich colour.
explain: Crimson can also describe a face. In Alice in Wonderland, the Queen turns crimson and screams «Off with her head!» She is so angry that her face goes deep red. The words around it, screams and Off with her head!, are the clue that crimson means rage, not shyness.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try red in place of crimson. Red still fits the cushion, but the Queen's furious face needs a stronger word, so the context shows you that crimson is the deeper, more dramatic choice.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Crimson» means a deep, strong red with a little blue in it.
fact: As a verb, «crimson» is rare and means to turn deep red, as when blushing.
fact: Crimson is deeper than scarlet, and it is one of the reds used in art.
fact: Phrases to know: «go crimson» means blush deep red, and «crimson with rage» means very angry.
exercise: «The Knave of Hearts carried the King's crown on a crimson velvet cushion.» What colour is the cushion? | Pure white | Bright blue | * A deep, strong red | Pale yellow
exercise: «The Queen turns crimson and screams, Off with her head!» What does crimson suggest here? | She is fast asleep | She is cold and her lips are blue | She is laughing and very happy | * Her face has gone deep red with anger
exercise: Which phrase tells you a person is very angry? | * Crimson with rage | Light as a feather | Quiet as a mouse | Cold as ice
test:
Crimson is which colour? | Pale blue | Yellow | * Deep red with a little blue in it | Bright green
A face that goes crimson is probably showing | Coldness | * Embarrassment or anger | Sleepiness | Hunger
exam:
In the procession, what was carried on the crimson velvet cushion? | A loaf of bread | A teapot | * The King's crown | A pair of gloves
